# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Mutex.new() mutual exclusion; m.lock()/m.unlock() serializes concurrent
#         function calls; queued waiters run in order after unlock.
# deferred: v1.x — Mutex stdlib type not in v1.0 scope
# matrix-row: stdlib-mutex
#
# Reason:
#   Mutex is a stdlib synchronization primitive scheduled for M6.  It depends on
#   ',' (OP_FORK_DETACH) for concurrent callers (M5 chk driver), the Lock
#   scheduler primitive for blocking acquire, and prototype-OOP method dispatch
#   for m.lock()/m.unlock() (M4).  All dependencies exceed M3 capability.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Mutex type and M5 chk driver):
# # var m = Mutex.new() | {};
# # function f(name) { ... m.lock(); sleep(1s); m.unlock() } | {};
# # m.lock(); f("func1"), sleep(1s); ... m.unlock();
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/mutex/basic.chk)
